    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0304" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1–2848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in India</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Donovan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-28T09:00:00+05:30">January 28, 1948—9
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Embtel 81, January 27.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d228-f1"/> Following substance conversation with Bajpai<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d228-f2"/> January 27 re Kashmir: GOI objects strongly to proposal withdraw Indian troops since in
                    their absence there will be no one to maintain law and order. If opposing troops
                    withdrew, GOI would reduce number its troops,
                    but Bajpai at no time indicated GOI would
                    consider withdrawal all Indian troops from what GOI considers Indian territory.</p>
                <p>
                    GOI cannot repudiate Sheikh Abdullah.</p>
                <p>
                    GOI feels national government should be formed
                    on basis adult franchise and, after formation this government, plebiscite should
                    be held with UN assistance. GOI will abide
                    results plebiscite.</p>
                <p>Russia has manifested no interest either at Delhi or Moscow in Kashmir.</p>
                <pb facs="0305" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/>
                <p>
                    GOI will under no circumstances consider
                    partition of Kashmir as “we have already gone through one partition.”</p>
                <p>Sent Department as 82, repeated Karachi 37. Department please repeat London
                    31.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donovan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
